00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
how many books have you read and  completely forgotten how many things  have you highlighted and underlined in a  book and just you know never looked at  again do you sometimes feel that it's  completely pointless to start reading  another book because you've never  actually used the one that you just  finished are you semi-anxious when you  are reading because you don't know what  to highlight or on the other end what  not to highlight because all of it just  feels completely pointless and useless  anyways well i find that these issues  come up again and again with reading and  i feel that at the crux of everything it  is an issue with the way that we are  processing our notes and the way that we  are reading in general especially  because i feel a lot of our reading is  done very very passively the thing that  works the most when reading often is  just our eyes and our brains are not  doing a lot of the work especially when  we are done with the book i think this  is a key time where you can make the  most out of everything you've just gone  through whenever we have an instinct  which i think as readers we're very very  familiar with to highlight or save  something all we do is just bold it or  underline it or highlight it somewhere  and let it be when in its essence  anything that provokes us to want to  save it is an opportunity for us to do a  thought exercise an opportunity for us  to have a discussion an opportunity for  us to create something think about  something change have a new learning  point and all we're doing with this is  completely letting it go so to combat  this issue i have a personal formula  that i use every single time that i read  a book and especially when i am done  reading this book and i wanted to share  it with you today and of all the crazy  over-the-top note-taking things that i  do this is one that i would genuinely  recommend to everyone who ever reads a  book it's not that complicated and i  have a free notion template if you just  want to download it somewhere but in  this video i'm going to go through  exactly how i use it why it is so useful  and why i feel it helps me so much with  retaining and learning more from the  books that i read all the time so let's  get started the first part of the  formula is the impressions bit and this  is something that is more of a stream of  consciousness it tends to be sentences  that i write here and there as i'm  reading a book based on the things that  i find interesting or the impressions  that i have from the book so this might  be things like oh i find this book to be  a bit condescending or i find this book  to be very very engaging i find it to be  life-changing i find the language to be  very entertaining or these are parts of  my life that i thought this book would  be the most useful at this would be  recommendations for the type of people  to read this book so this is just like a  general vague impression you can think  of it as kind of a summary in the  newspaper or a recommendation or a  restaurant review so this is the kind of  tone that i will put in this part of the  reflection and i will fill it in as i am  reading the book it will usually be  three to five sentences in general but  it's enough for me to look at every time  that i go back to my book reviews and go  aha yeah i remember what i felt like  when i was reading the book because very  often i forget this impression that i  have now the second part is the key part  of the note-taking process and this is  the actionable takeaways in the past  when i used to read books all i used to  do is keep notes from the books which  would be just highlights or comments on  the things that i was highlighting but i  made this sort of mindset shift when i  thought i'm not finding books useful i'm  not seeing that they are changing my  life and i think the reason for that is  that i'm not applying anything or  looking at things in a book in a way  that i can apply them to my personal  life so at this stage what i decided was  that every single time that i found  something interesting in a book or  highlightable in a book i would take a  second either while i am reading or if  i'm in the flow or in the zone after i'm  done with the book and think about how  this can be applied to a change for my  life so i have to think of actively how  can i apply this to me so for example if  i was reading a book about creativity  and the author was talking about this  famous writer who every night before he  went to bed dreamed of something to look  forward to the next day and this really  impacted the way that he works i won't  just underline this i will actively turn  this into a sentence that is applicable  to me so i will say go to sleep every  day with something you're looking  forward to the next morning because this  will make you more happy to wake up and  eventually your day will be filled of  things that you are looking forward to  doing so even by just changing the words  in this highlight i am converting it  into something i can personally use  rather than just a story about someone  else's life and i will go very overboard  with this in this actionable takeaways  bit i will convert everything that i  find interesting in a book into  something that i can apply to my own  life or to other people's lives  otherwise it will not go in this section  so every single note i'm underlining i'm  converting it in my mind into this thing  and also another thing that i like to do  is i keep this only to 10 quotes which  can be extremely difficult for long and  interesting books and the reason for  this is to me  i can underline and highlight hundreds  and hundreds of pieces of information  from a book but it's unlikely therefore  that i will use these so i will keep it  only to my top ten i can highlight other  things and i will put this in an archive  in my book notes so in the bottom will  be all the things that i found  interesting but i will only keep 10  things in this bit of actionable  takeaways and that means that sometimes  i will remove things from it to add  something else but in the end of the day  when i look at my book notes i only want  10 very important ones for each book  that can actually change my life and in  this way i'm approaching the book in a  very active way of thinking rather than  just passively reading the book i'm  thinking okay how can this be applied to  me i use this for fiction too even when  i see characters say things that are  interesting do things that are  interesting when they have a new bit of  insight or when i get to understand the  way that their brains work i start to  think oh can this be applicable to me  and i will still turn this into an  actionable takeaway part number three is  quite straightforward and this is my  favorite quotes from the book and these  are things that can be mentioned and  converted in the actual takeaways to  something else but there are phrases and  words that author has put together so  beautifully that i just want to preserve  them the way they are because either i  might use them in presentations videos  pieces of writing or creation that i  make in the future or i just want to see  them because they're so powerful that i  don't want to paraphrase them myself so  this will usually be three to five maybe  ten if it's a very long very amazing  book of literal quotes that i will take  from the book and i want to save the way  that they are and lastly i have a bonus  section and this is for the books that  are really really groundbreaking  sometimes they will have multiple  questions or a formula that i really  really want to preserve the way that it  is i read this book recently that was  talking about letting go of things and  of loss and it had three very important  questions that you can ask yourself  every time that you lose something and i  think there was something along the  lines of um did you know that you were  going to lose this thing at some point  in the near future how much more time  would you want to have had with this  thing and lastly do you feel that you  are worth any less now that you don't  have this so this three-part formula i  thought was really really kind of strong  and groundbreaking for me so i thought i  wanted to preserve this in the way that  it was in the bonus sections so either  it can be something like this or it can  be advice that a character gives another  character that i find is really really  helpful and sometimes these are  scattered throughout the book or there  will be a character arc or a character  growth arc for someone that i will break  down into steps and i will turn this  into a formula that i will add to my  bonus section because it is in way an  actionable takeaway but it has multiple  steps so it's really interesting and  these are small parts that i can just  keep separate and look at them sometimes  so whenever i'm done with a book i now  have this kind of notion page that has  all of this information on the book so  it kind of has my first impressions on  it and who i would recommend it to then  it has the actionable takeaways 10  things or 10 ways that this book can  change my life then it has some favorite  quotes from the book and these used  these are a lot less than i used to take  before i'm very picky with these now  then i would go into the bonus materials  or anything extra in the book that i  felt was a formula or something that i  want to apply to my life a lot and yep  in this way i feel as though my reading  becomes a lot more active than it used  to be in the past it's not just me kind  of rushing through books and not  thinking about them but i'm really  thinking about how can this add  something to my life that i can hold on  for a very long time and i've genuinely  found that it has made reading and  note-taking so much more pleasurable for  me and also so much more beneficial for  me if you're interested in books i  actually share my summaries broken down  in this form in a free newsletter which  will be linked somewhere down below so  as i read books i very often share some  of them here with you all you can also  download this notion page formula for  free in my description if you have any  note-taking tips i am always very very  keen on knowing about them or any books  that you want to recommend otherwise  thank you so much for spending this time  with me i hope you have a wonderful rest  of your day find a brilliant book to  read and don't believe everything you  think thanks bye

